This study introduces an innovative task that merges three-dimensional (3D) shape creation with virtual reality (VR) interactions to enhance 3D shape retrieval. Our research explores how conventional 3D modeling tools can be utilized in immersive VR environments, leveraging drawing skills to retrieve relevant 3D shapes. We developed two novel interfaces that allow users to create and manipulate 3D shapes using VR, and conducted a user study involving 29 participants who created and retrieved shapes using our proposed interfaces. Our results demonstrate that conventional 3D modeling skills can effectively enable 3D shape retrieval in immersive VR settings. The associated code and models are publicly accessible for research purposes. Additionally, a demo video is available on Google Drive for demonstration purposes. 

